# UNBURY (General Description). The minor cycle whose position is given
# in TS 31 is taken to be position of the next instruction.
#
# The report gives this description and no table. This table is ours.
# TS 31 is first moved back one minor cycle, to the most recent note. The
# note is the position of the B that entered the subsidiary, so we go on at
# the instruction after it. Only TS 2, 4, 5 and 6 are altered.
UNBURY
  1   TS 31 - TS 2
  3   ADD 'A'
  4   UNBURY 40 - TS 2
  6   SUBTRACT
  7   TS 4 - TS 31
  9   UNBURY 41 - TS 2
 11   ADD
 12   TS 4 - TS 6
 13   B, 1
 14   TS 6 - TS 2
 15   ADD 'A'
 16   UNBURY 42 - TS 2
 18   ADD
 19   TS 4 - TS 6
 20   B, 1
# UNBURY 13 carries out the instruction just made, which fetches the note.
# The numbers: a pulse in digit 18; the code of type L; and a pulse in
# digit 19 with the digits of type B.
 40   0000,0000,0000,0000,0100,0000,0000,0000
 41   0000,0101,0000,0000,0000,0000,0000,0000
 42   0110,0000,0000,0000,0010,0000,0000,0000
